Q) How do Docker containers communicate with each other?
A) Containers attached to the same user-defined bridge network can communicate using Docker's built-in DNS. Instead of using IP addresses or localhost, services communicate using their Compose service names, such as mysql or redis. This avoids hardcoded IPs and allows containers to be recreated without changing application configuration.

